<h2>Interim bail and its verification problem</h2>
<p>Medical-ground interim bail turns on verification. Here, the court had before it a verification report with awkward findings: the surgery first scheduled for 13 October 2026 did not happen, the father did not report to the hospital that day, and no fresh consultation or new date was sought until mid-November. When counsel stated the surgery was now definitively fixed for 20 November 2026 &mdash; a date the State confirmed &mdash; the court had to weigh a genuine family emergency against a record that invited caution.</p>

<h2>The balance the court struck</h2>
<div class="compare">
  <div class="col old"><strong>What release would have meant.</strong> One month outside custody for an accused facing MCOCA Sections 3/4 allegations, four other pending cases, and a Section 18 MCOCA confessional statement describing him as a shooter, recruiter and facilitator of a syndicate.</div>
  <div class="arrow">&rarr;</div>
  <div class="col new"><strong>What custody parole achieves.</strong> Presence at the father&rsquo;s bedside on every day that matters &mdash; the eve of surgery, the surgery, and up to seven days of hospitalisation &mdash; under escort, with the State&rsquo;s custody never interrupted.</div>
</div>

<h2>The fine print of the order</h2>
<p>The conditions repay attention because they form a template. The applicant leaves jail at 9:00 AM and returns by 6:00 PM &mdash; a nine-hour window; he remains in the custody of a plain-clothes escort throughout; he may meet his father, family and friends at the hospital but no co-accused in any ongoing case; he may carry no mobile phone; and he may visit no place other than the hospital. Crucially, the order is self-verifying: the investigating officer must confirm with the hospital that surgery is listed for 20 November and inform the Jail Superintendent by 6 PM the previous evening, failing which the order simply does not operate and a fresh application is the only route.</p>

<h2>Where this fits in bail practice</h2>
<div class="flow">
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Credibility is cumulative.</strong> Shifting medical dates in successive applications damage the grant of interim bail more than almost anything else; records should be aligned with the hospital before filing.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Ask for the middle remedy.</strong> Where the offence is grave, pleading custody parole in the alternative &mdash; with a realistic schedule tied to hospital events &mdash; gives the court a workable option short of release.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Know the rules.</strong> Rule 1209 of the Delhi Prison Rules governs custody parole for undertrials; the six-hour reference in Rule 1203 can yield to the occasion, but the escort, expense and verification architecture stays intact.</div>
</div>
<p>In stringent-statute cases &mdash; MCOCA, NDPS commercial quantity, UAPA &mdash; this order illustrates the realistic ceiling of medical-ground relief in Delhi: not liberty, but presence.</p>
<div class="note">This article reports an order of the High Court of Delhi for general information only. It is not legal advice and does not comment on any pending proceeding.</div>
